# Workbench data + model binaries are LOCAL ONLY. They are large, and data/ holds your real
# documents. Never commit them. The folder STRUCTURE and the docs DO get committed, so a fresh
# clone shows every drop point.

# Ignore the contents...
models/**
data/**
reports/**

# ...but keep descending into subdirectories. Without these, git never walks into an excluded
# directory, and the !README.md rule below would silently never match.
!models/**/
!data/**/
!reports/**/

# Structure + docs survive.
!**/README.md
!**/.gitkeep

# The repo-root .gitignore has a global `*.txt` rule (for the scratch logs littering the root).
# These workbench text files are real source and must survive it.
!requirements.txt
!**/CHECKSUMS.txt
!**/LICENSES.md
